WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.550
Find a steady seated or resting position.

2
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.000
This practice works with ordinary self-critical thoughts.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:14.790
Choose a mild example, not the most painful judgment you carry, and return to neutral sensation whenever needed.

4
00:00:22.507 --> 00:00:24.927
Feel the body's contact with support.

5
00:00:26.627 --> 00:00:30.557
Notice the room, one sound, and the natural movement of breathing.

6
00:00:32.257 --> 00:00:35.757
These are present before any thought is examined.

7
00:00:51.833 --> 00:00:54.743
Recall a recent moment when an inner critical voice appeared.

8
00:00:56.443 --> 00:01:01.163
Keep the situation at a distance, like a short headline rather than a detailed replay.

9
00:01:17.239 --> 00:01:19.299
Notice one sentence the critic used.

10
00:01:20.999 --> 00:01:26.189
Perhaps it began with you always, you never, you should, or you are not enough.

11
00:01:27.889 --> 00:01:30.059
Hear it as a sentence, not a verdict.

12
00:01:49.351 --> 00:01:53.271
Add a simple frame: I am noticing the thought that.

13
00:01:54.971 --> 00:01:56.941
Then repeat only the core idea.

14
00:01:58.641 --> 00:02:02.841
See whether this creates even a little room around the words.

15
00:02:25.347 --> 00:02:26.557
Feel the feet or hands again.

16
00:02:28.257 --> 00:02:31.267
A thought can be loud while the body is also touching something solid.

17
00:02:32.967 --> 00:02:34.487
Both facts can exist at once.

18
00:02:53.779 --> 00:03:01.479
Ask what the critical thought may be trying to prevent: failure, rejection, embarrassment, uncertainty, or loss of control.

19
00:03:03.179 --> 00:03:07.489
Understanding a protective aim does not make the harsh method useful.

20
00:03:29.996 --> 00:03:31.266
Notice the tone.

21
00:03:32.966 --> 00:03:37.276
Would the same information be clearer without contempt, exaggeration, or insult?

22
00:03:38.976 --> 00:03:41.976
Separate any practical message from the way it was delivered.

23
00:04:04.482 --> 00:04:07.452
Translate the thought into specific, workable language.

24
00:04:09.152 --> 00:04:15.142
Instead of I ruin everything, perhaps: one part did not go as planned, and I can decide what to repair.

25
00:04:16.842 --> 00:04:18.582
Use facts you can verify.

26
00:04:44.304 --> 00:04:46.214
Let that revised sentence settle.

27
00:04:47.914 --> 00:04:49.294
It does not need to be positive.

28
00:04:50.994 --> 00:04:54.304
It needs to be accurate enough to guide the next step without attacking your worth.

29
00:05:16.811 --> 00:05:19.901
If the critic argues back, notice another thought.

30
00:05:21.601 --> 00:05:24.301
You do not need to win a debate.

31
00:05:26.001 --> 00:05:29.651
Return to contact with support and repeat the more accurate wording once.

32
00:05:52.158 --> 00:06:00.068
Consider whether the situation belongs to your responsibility, someone else's responsibility, shared responsibility, or simple uncertainty.

33
00:06:01.768 --> 00:06:04.428
Do not take more ownership than the facts support.

34
00:06:26.935 --> 00:06:30.785
Name one thing you can do, learn, ask, repair, or leave alone.

35
00:06:32.485 --> 00:06:34.085
Keep it small enough to be real.

36
00:06:35.785 --> 00:06:39.485
If no action is possible now, recognizing that limit can be accurate too.

37
00:07:05.207 --> 00:07:10.377
Try a respectful response: I can take responsibility without reducing myself to this moment.

38
00:07:12.077 --> 00:07:15.857
Adjust the words so they fit your values and the actual situation.

39
00:07:38.363 --> 00:07:41.993
Notice any change in shoulders, jaw, breath, or belly.

40
00:07:43.693 --> 00:07:47.463
There may be relief, resistance, no change, or a mixture.

41
00:07:49.163 --> 00:07:51.933
The body's response is information, not a score.

42
00:08:11.225 --> 00:08:13.975
Imagine hearing the critical sentence again later today.

43
00:08:15.675 --> 00:08:22.535
Rehearse three moves: recognize it as a thought, find the factual message, choose a respectful next sentence.

44
00:08:51.472 --> 00:08:52.822
Let the example fade.

45
00:08:54.522 --> 00:08:58.072
Return to sounds, light, and the whole body's position.

46
00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:04.112
You are more than the thought, and you do not need that claim to feel inspiring for it to be accurate.

47
00:09:23.404 --> 00:09:27.404
Offer one closing phrase: clear is more useful than cruel.

48
00:09:29.104 --> 00:09:31.354
Or choose your own brief reminder.

49
00:09:33.054 --> 00:09:35.844
Let it accompany one natural breath.

50
00:09:51.920 --> 00:09:53.180
Move when ready.

51
00:09:54.880 --> 00:10:00.000
You practiced listening for useful information without handing a harsh voice authority over your value.
